Below is a practical, step‑by‑step playbook you can follow (or adapt) to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole pipeline – from concept to deployment – and sprinkle in concrete code snippets, tool recommendations, and best‑practice tips.

---

## 1️⃣  Define the Scope & Gather Requirements

| What | Why | How |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Target audience** | Determines design language, accessibility needs, and device mix | User personas, analytics review |
| **Core features** | Shopping cart, product catalog, search, filters, checkout, user account, reviews, admin panel | Feature list, MoSCoW prioritization |
| **Performance goals** | Fast first paint, low bundle size | Lighthouse targets, critical‑path CSS |
| **SEO & PWA** | Organic traffic, offline support | Server‑side rendering, service workers |
| **Compliance** | GDPR, PCI‑DSS, WCAG | Legal audit, privacy policy, accessible components |

> **Tip:** Create a *Product Requirements Document* (PRD) that captures all of the above. It becomes the single source of truth for designers, developers, and stakeholders.

---

## 2️⃣  Choose the Tech Stack

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React** (most ecosystem) |
| **State Management** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, Vuex | **Redux Toolkit** (simple, typed, devtools) |
| **Routing** | React Router, Next.js, Vue Router | **Next.js** (SSR + SSG + API routes) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Tailwind CSS, Styled‑Components | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **Component Library** | Material‑UI, Ant Design, Chakra UI | **Chakra UI** (accessibility out‑of‑the‑box) |
| **Build Tool** | Vite, Webpack, Next.js | **Next.js** (built‑in Vite‑like dev server) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | **Jest + RTL** for unit, **Cypress** for E2E |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Vercel | **Vercel** (native Next.js deployment) |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Segment | **Plausible** (privacy‑friendly) |
| **Payment** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (modern API, strong docs) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Built‑in SSR/SSG → SEO & fast load times  
> • API routes → lightweight backend for auth, cart, etc.  
> • File‑based routing → zero config

---

## 3️⃣  Design & Prototyping

1. **Wireframes** – Sketch low‑fidelity screens (Home, Category, Product, Cart, Checkout, Account).  
2. **High‑fidelity mockups** – Use Figma or Adobe XD.  
3. **Component library** – Build a design system (colors, typography, spacing, tokens).  
4. **Accessibility audit** – Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance (contrast, focus, ARIA).  
5. **User testing** – Conduct quick usability tests on prototypes.

> **Pro tip:** Export design tokens directly into your CSS framework (e.g., Tailwind config) to keep design consistent.

---

## 4️⃣  Project Skeleton (Next.js + TypeScript)

```bash
npx create-next-app@latest ecommerce-frontend --typescript
cd ecommerce-frontend
npm install @chakra-ui/react @emotion/react @emotion/styled framer-motion
npm install tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

**`tailwind.config.js`**

```js
module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./pages/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
    "./components/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}
```

**`pages/_app.tsx`**

```tsx
import { ChakraProvider } from "@chakra-ui/react";
import "../styles/globals.css";

function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
  return (
    <ChakraProvider>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </ChakraProvider>
  );
}

export default MyApp;
```

---

## 5️⃣  Core Pages & Components

### 5.1  Layout

```tsx
// components/Layout.tsx
import { Box, Flex, Heading, Spacer, Link } from "@chakra-ui/react";
import NextLink from "next/link";

export const Layout = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => (
  <Flex direction="column" minH="100vh">
    <Box as="header" bg="teal.500" color="white" py={4}>
      <Flex maxW="1200px" mx="auto" px={4} align="center">
        <Heading size="md">ShopEase</Heading>
        <Spacer />
        <NextLink href="/cart" passHref>
          <Link>Cart</Link>
        </NextLink>
      </Flex>
    </Box>
    <Box as="main" flex="1" maxW="1200px" mx="auto" px={4} py={6}>
      {children}
    </Box>
    <Box as="footer" bg="gray.200" py={4} textAlign="center">
      © 2026 ShopEase
    </Box>
  </Flex>
);
```

### 5.2  Product Card

```tsx
// components/ProductCard.tsx
import { Box, Image, Text, Button } from "@chakra-ui/react";
import NextLink from "next/link";

export const ProductCard = ({
  id,
  title,
  price,
  image,
}: {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  image: string;
}) => (
  <Box borderWidth="1px" borderRadius="lg" overflow="hidden" p={4}>
    <Image src={image} alt={title} objectFit="cover" h="200px" w="100%" />
    <Text mt={2} fontWeight="bold">{title}</Text>
    <Text color="teal.600">${price.toFixed(2)}</Text>
    <NextLink href={`/product/${id}`} passHref>
      <Button mt={2} colorScheme="teal" size="sm">
        View
      </Button>
    </NextLink>
  </Box>
);
```

### 5.3  Home Page (SSR + SSG)

```tsx
// pages/index.tsx
import { GetStaticProps } from "next";
import { Grid } from "@chakra-ui/react";
import { ProductCard } from "../components/ProductCard";

export default function Home({ products }) {
  return (
    <Grid templateColumns="repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr))" gap={6}>
      {products.map((p) => (
        <ProductCard key={p.id} {...p} />
      ))}
    </Grid>
  );
}

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async () => {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/products");
  const products = await res.json();
  return { props: { products } };
};
```

---

## 6️⃣  State Management (Cart & Auth)

### 6.1  Cart Slice (Redux Toolkit)

```ts
// store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";

interface CartItem {
  productId: string;
  quantity: number;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: "cart",
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addItem(state, action: PayloadAction<CartItem>) {
      const existing = state.items.find((i) => i.productId === action.payload.productId);
      if (existing) existing.quantity += action.payload.quantity;
      else state.items.push(action.payload);
    },
    removeItem(state, action: PayloadAction<string>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter((i) => i.productId !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

### 6.2  Store Setup

```ts
// store/store.ts
import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import cartReducer from "./cartSlice";

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: { cart: cartReducer },
});

export type RootState = ReturnType<typeof store.getState>;
export type AppDispatch = typeof store.dispatch;
```

### 6.3  Provider

```tsx
// pages/_app.tsx
import { Provider } from "react-redux";
import { store } from "../store/store";

function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
  return (
    <Provider store={store}>
      <ChakraProvider>
        <Component {...pageProps} />
      </ChakraProvider>
    </Provider>
  );
}
```

---

## 7️⃣  API Integration

| Feature | Endpoint | Method | Notes |
|---------|----------|--------|-------|
| Products | `/api/products` | GET | Paginated, filterable |
| Cart | `/api/cart` | POST/GET/DELETE | Session‑based |
| Checkout | `/api/checkout` | POST | Stripe webhook |
| Auth | `/api/auth/*` | OAuth / JWT | NextAuth.js |

> **NextAuth.js** is a great choice for authentication (email/password, Google, GitHub, etc.) and integrates seamlessly with Next.js.

---

## 8️⃣  Payment Flow (Stripe)

1. **Create a Checkout Session** (API route)

```ts
// pages/api/checkout.ts
import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from "next";
import Stripe from "stripe";

const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!, { apiVersion: "2024-04-10" });

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  if (req.method !== "POST") return res.status(405).end();

  const { items } = req.body; // [{ priceId, quantity }]
  try {
    const session = await stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
      payment_method_types: ["card"],
      line_items: items.map((i) => ({
        price: i.priceId,
        quantity: i.quantity,
      })),
      mode: "payment",
      success_url: `${req.headers.origin}/success?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}`,
      cancel_url: `${req.headers.origin}/cart`,
    });
    res.json({ url: session.url });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

2. **Redirect to Stripe** (client side)

```tsx
// components/CheckoutButton.tsx
import { useRouter } from "next/router";
import { Button } from "@chakra-ui/react";

export const CheckoutButton = () => {
  const router = useRouter();

  const handleCheckout = async () => {
    const res = await fetch("/api/checkout", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({ items: /* cart items */ }),
    });
    const { url } = await res.json();
    window.location.href = url;
  };

  return <Button colorScheme="teal" onClick={handleCheckout}>Checkout</Button>;
};
```

3. **Handle Webhooks** (for order confirmation, inventory updates)

```ts
// pages/api/webhooks/stripe.ts
import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from "next";
import Stripe from "stripe";

const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!, { apiVersion: "2024-04-10" });

export const config = { api: { bodyParser: false } };

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  const sig = req.headers["stripe-signature"] as string;
  let event: Stripe.Event;

  try {
    event = stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(req.body, sig, process.env.STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET!);
  } catch (err) {
    return res.status(400).send(`Webhook Error: ${err.message}`);
  }

  if (event.type === "checkout.session.completed") {
    const session = event.data.object as Stripe.Checkout.Session;
    // TODO: Fulfill order, update DB, send email
  }

  res.json({ received: true });
}
```

